<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duchy of Croatia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dalmatian Croatia, Littoral Croatia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, also called Dalmatian or Littoral Croatia, was a medieval Slavic principality in the hinterland of the Dalmatian coast, formed in the late 8th and 9th centuries under Frankish and later Byzantine influence. Its rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trpimirovic-dynasty">Trpimirović dynasty</a>, such as Trpimir and Branimir, extended its power, and around 925 Tomislav united it with Pannonian Croatia to form the Kingdom of Croatia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duchy-of-croatia.jpg" alt="Duchy of Croatia" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hxseek 03:42, 15 January 2009 (UTC) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balkans850.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
